// Obfusku Canonical Example: Host and File System I/O
//
// Demonstrates:
// 1. Console printing via native `print : ⌘ → ∅`.
// 2. Sandboxed file reading via native `readFile : ⌘ → ⌘`.
// 3. Sandboxed file writing via native `writeFile : ⌘ → (⌘ → ∅)`.
// 4. Interactive input note: `readLine : ∅ → ⌘` reads a line from stdin,
//    raising Failure("EOF", ...) when the input stream terminates.

// 1. Console printing
header ≔ "=== Obfusku I/O Subsystem ==="
loggedHeader ≔ print(header)

// 2. Sandboxed file reading (scoped to the script directory)
initialData ≔ readFile("sample_message.txt")
loggedInitial ≔ print(initialData)

// 3. Sandboxed file writing
// `writeFile` is curried: writeFile(path)(content) -> ∅
writeStatus ≔ writeFile("sample_message.txt")("Obfusku host I/O successfully verified.")

// 4. Verify written file contents
verifiedData ≔ readFile("sample_message.txt")
loggedVerified ≔ print(verifiedData)

// Final returned result
result ≔ verifiedData
❧
